\caption(Original Hasse-interval proxy with its interpretation corrected.)
\alttext(Actual complete integer smoothness counts are plotted as isolated observations; no theoretical per-curve success probability or monotonicity is inferred.)

> Limits and verification

All modulus products use exact unsigned128 intermediates, correcting the former
signed128 overflow on large unsigned64 residues. This is a fixed-width native
implementation requiring compiler128-bit integers, not an arbitrary-precision
cryptographic tool. Zero and one return themselves; small primes can also return
themselves; exhausted composites return n too. The proper flag distinguishes an
actual divisor from failure, but failure is never a primality proof and a found
factor can be composite. Zero curve budget is an explicit trial-division-only
control.

Explicit bound is in[2,1000000], curve attempts at most1000000. Count-only
analysis performs no optional history capture. Trace cap defaults to one million
actual prime-power/curve/denominator records, checked before each append;0
disables only that optional cap. Unknown future work is not fabricated as a
preallocated history. Fields, point components, capacities, output/runtime
copies and bytes are excluded. Quota failure returns no partial result. No
external dataset is relevant to exact factorization controls.

Independent arbitrary-precision modular arithmetic verified100 bounded seeded
studies,144 actual curves,3862 evaluated denominator records and100 full
unsigned64 doubling controls, including on-curve operands, PRNG words, GCDs,
inverse slopes and produced points. Complete smoothness counts on all eight
original Hasse intervals were independently trial-factored. Another100 default
searches matched frozen defined-range factors exactly. Native tests cover
original factors, the tiny failed inverse, explicit exhaustion/noncertificate
cases, actual work/quotas and full-range guards. The complete ten-report batch
passed77 native CTest cases,39 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases,106
compiled/executed public examples,479/479 scoped definitions and ten
representative clangd hovers. All4 complete report programs executed and all4
native figures were visually reviewed. HTML/Markdown computed result and
identical source/build/export figure bytes passed verification. Repeatable
receipts are retained under `build/mepml-conversion/batch-194-203/`.

> References

H. W. Lenstra Jr.(1987),
[Factoring Integers with Elliptic Curves|https://doi.org/10.2307/1971363],
Annals of Mathematics126(3),649–673. This report demonstrates a bounded affine
stage1 implementation and carefully distinguishes its evidence from the paper’s
broader complexity analysis and production ECM variants.
